timeline.body:
@henningandersen so for now I got by with constraining the catch by doing the following fixes:

* https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/65415/commits/526777087b04ec4a63ead3accdefb2178f224deb (catch the exception we throw on an uninitialized client or if an action is missing by catching `IllegalStateException` (the change in ex. type here is just a revert of a prior attempt at fixing this by just using `IllegalArgumentException` sine we already catch that but I threw that approach out), fix watcher bug in serializing exceptions https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/65415/commits/adf535de770cf3519fbc04ceed522f48ed628138 and fix CCR bug that had an exception bubble up all the way in https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/65415/commits/7be5d1c445dd62a1f2282f49cd738c42b97dc2b2)

wdyt? Good to go with this one or should be tread more carefully maybe and fix these issue separately in follow-ups and keep catching `Exception` initially maybe? (especially thinking about the `7.10` backport here)
